  │    "S": null,
  │    "E": null,
  │    "W": "DZ",
  │    "text": "Riga is the eastern end of the known world for most Hanseatic sailors, and the beginning of it for the men who come down the river from the forest interior carrying amber and furs and strange quiet faces. The Livonian Order built this city on a bend in the Daugava river. They still run it, after a fashion — though the Hansa factors have their own quarter now, their own church, their own courts.\n\nThe amber market opens at dawn and closes when the amber runs out, which is never. It comes in on river barges from somewhere deep in the forest that no Hansa man has seen and returned from able to describe it. The forest people trade in amber and silence. Both are worth more than the sailors understand.",
  │    "npc": null,
  │    "battle": null,
  │    "loot": null,
